{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559544-pantheon-specific-purviews-for-deities-that-cross-pantheons","id":1559544,"title":"Pantheon Specific Purviews for Deities that Cross Pantheons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-21T02:09:04-07:00","id":1559544,"title":"Pantheon Specific Purviews for Deities that Cross Pantheons","content":"Here\u2019s a question that\u2019s been bugging me: For gods who have mantles in more than one pantheon, do they use their \u201cnative\u201d Pantheon Specific Purview (PSP), or the PSP of the pantheon they\u2019re presenting in? What about their Scions?<br /> <br /> For instance, Anat is a goddess of the Ilhm (Phoenician/Canaanite) pantheon, but she also became a prominent goddess of the Netjer (Egyptian) pantheon, beginning around the time of the Hyksos invasion.<br /> <br /> When Anat is interacting with the World in her Netjer Mantle, does she have access to the Netjer PSP? Would Scions of her Netjer Mantle inherit the Netjer PSP or the Ilhm PSP?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-21T05:46:45-07:00","id":1559545,"title":"","content":"I fix this with Mantles; Pantheon membership is tied to the deity's Mantle, so to be in different Pantheons, you need a separate Mantle for each.<br /> <br /> I don't remember 'how membership in multiple Pantheons actually works' ever being officially addressed though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-21T12:44:32-07:00","id":1559547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559544-pantheon-specific-purviews-for-deities-that-cross-pantheons?p=1559545#post1559545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fix this with Mantles; Pantheon membership is tied to the deity's Mantle, so to be in different Pantheons, you need a separate Mantle for each.<br /> <br /> I don't remember 'how membership in multiple Pantheons actually works' ever being officially addressed though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It gets referred to in the descriptions of some deities (Ishtar is listed as being in a few different pantheons under the name of Astarte), but I haven't seen it addressed from a game mechanics sense.<br /> <br /> I've been running it that different Mantles can have different Purviews, and different PSPs if they are in a different pantheon, and that Scions inherit Purviews from their parent's Mantle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-21T14:38:07-07:00","id":1559550,"title":"","content":"Given that the Greek and Egyptian pantheons are two of the most popular in the game (only the Norse pantheon has as wide a popularity) Hermes Trimagistos needs to be addressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T08:48:58-07:00","id":1559564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1559544-pantheon-specific-purviews-for-deities-that-cross-pantheons?p=1559550#post1559550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the Greek and Egyptian pantheons are two of the most popular in the game (only the Norse pantheon has as wide a popularity) Hermes Trimagistos needs to be addressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my game, Hermes introduced his Scion to Hermes Trimagistos, implying that Trimagistos was one of his aspects (mantles). Of course, this was Hermes, god of trickery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28946-pryderi","name":"Pryderi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}